  "_comment": [
    "Every address the old WordPress site publishes, and where it should land on the new one.",
    "",
    "Taken from the live sitemaps at templeofsun.com on 30 August 2026, so this is what",
    "actually exists, not a guess. Google has these addresses indexed. Without this file",
    "every one of them becomes a 404 the moment the domain switches over, and the search",
    "ranking they have built up is thrown away.",
    "",
    "Add a line here, run tools/prepare-for-upload.py, and _redirects is rebuilt.",
    "Never edit _redirects by hand: it is overwritten on every run.",
    "",
    "'exact' runs first and wins. 'catchall' is the safety net underneath, for any old",
    "address that was never in a sitemap. Cloudflare takes the first line that matches,",
    "so order matters and the script preserves it.",
    "",
    "Everything is 301 (permanent), which is what passes the old ranking to the new page."
  ],

